# SolarDoctor — backend environment template
# (legacy AXALON_* names still work; SOLARDOCTOR_* wins when both are set)
# Copy to .env on the server:  cp .env.example .env  (then fill in real values)
# Loaded by the FastAPI backend (solardoctor.api.app).

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev (default): leave unset → sqlite:///solardoctor.db
# Production (Supabase Postgres): use the URI from
#   Supabase → Project Settings → Database → Connection string (URI)
#   and prefix the driver with postgresql+psycopg2://
# SOLARDOCTOR_DB_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@db.YOURREF.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Modes: off | apikey | users. The frontend login page needs `users` (email + password accounts).
# If unset: `apikey` when SOLARDOCTOR_API_KEY is set, otherwise `off` (wide open).
SOLARDOCTOR_AUTH_MODE=users
# Legacy shared key (only for AUTH_MODE=apikey; leave unset in users mode):
# SOLARDOCTOR_API_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-secret

# `make seed` creates admin@solardoctor.example and technician@solardoctor.example.
# Set passwords here (min length per policy; do NOT reuse real passwords) or leave them
# unset: they are then generated and printed ONCE by the seed script.
# SOLARDOCTOR_SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# SOLARDOCTOR_SEED_TECH_PASSWORD=
# Seeding without network (CI): make seed SEED_ARGS=--offline

# ── CORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated allowed origins. axalonsystems.com is already a default;
# set this only if your frontend lives on a different domain.
# SOLARDOCTOR_CORS_ORIGINS=https://axalonsystems.com,https://www.axalonsystems.com

# ── Inference ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set true ONLY on the Jetson after exporting best.engine (TensorRT).
# On a CPU cloud VM (Oracle), leave this false — it uses best.pt.
SOLARDOCTOR_USE_ENGINE=false

# ── Storage / housekeeping (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# SOLARDOCTOR_OUTPUT_DIR=output
# SOLARDOCTOR_RESULTS_TTL_HOURS=24

# ── Fault alerts (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sent when an inspection job finds faults at or above SOLARDOCTOR_ALERT_MIN_SEVERITY.
# Each channel is enabled only when configured. Test via Settings → Send test alert.
# SOLARDOCTOR_ALERT_MIN_SEVERITY=CRITICAL          # CRITICAL | HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
# SOLARDOCTOR_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://axalonsystems.com
# Webhook (Slack incoming-webhook URLs work as-is):
# SOLARDOCTOR_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXX/YYY/ZZZ
# Email (SMTP, STARTTLS by default):
# SOLARDOCTOR_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SOLARDOCTOR_SMTP_PORT=587
# SOLARDOCTOR_SMTP_USER=alerts@example.com
# SOLARDOCTOR_SMTP_PASSWORD=change-me
# SOLARDOCTOR_SMTP_STARTTLS=true
# SOLARDOCTOR_ALERT_EMAIL_FROM=alerts@example.com
# SOLARDOCTOR_ALERT_EMAIL_TO=ops@example.com,oncall@example.com

# ── Orthomosaic generation (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# NodeODM server used to stitch drone images into GeoTIFF orthos from the Park Map.
# Unset → feature disabled (the UI explains why). See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# SOLARDOCTOR_NODEODM_URL=http://localhost:3001
# SOLARDOCTOR_NODEODM_TOKEN=

# ── Error monitoring (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry is enabled only when SENTRY_DSN is set. Query-string credentials
# (api_key, token, share) are masked before events leave the process.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1
# SENTRY_PROFILE_SAMPLE_RATE=0
# SENTRY_SEND_PII=false

# ── Thermal detector (YOLO11x, AGPL-3.0 weights) ───────────────────────────────
# Weights are NOT in git. `make weights` downloads them from Hugging Face.
ENABLE_THERMAL=false
# SOLARDOCTOR_THERMAL_REPO=solar-doctor/solar-doctor-thermal-yolo11x
# HF_TOKEN=            # only for uploading weights or reading a private repo

# ── Frontend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make dev` / `make web` set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL to http://localhost:$API_PORT automatically.
# Set it here only when the API lives elsewhere (it is baked in at `next build`):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
